# acp — overview

REQUIRES: krunvm, WB_ACP_EXPERIMENTAL=1, a connected coding agent OS: macOS (libkrun/HVF) COST: the agent runs against the user's own subscription

Reach for `acp` when a task is better handed to a full external coding agent (Codex / Claude Code) than done inline — a long, autonomous, multi-file change on a worktree. The external agent runs in an isolated local microVM; you hand it a task and a worktree and collect the edits.

EXPERIMENTAL, local-only. If no coding agent is connected, do NOT use this — tell the user to connect one in the desktop (Settings → Integrations) first.

